{
  "format": [
    "Shared test vectors of the SQL text scanner (sql-queries-design.md decisions 4 and 6). The engine's SqlTextTests and the editor's",
    "scanner tests both read this file; a change to either scanner changes this file first.",
    "Each case: name; dialect (postgresql, sqlserver, mysql, sqlite, oracle); text; and what the scanner must answer:",
    "placeholders: every :name placeholder in text order, each {name, offset, line, column}: offset of the colon in UTF-16 code units",
    "  from 0, line and column from 1 (lines end at \\n, columns count UTF-16 code units).",
    "firstWord: the first word outside comments, upper-cased, leading ( skipped; null when the first token is anything else.",
    "verb: firstWord, or when it is WITH the first of SELECT INSERT UPDATE DELETE MERGE REPLACE VALUES TABLE at the WITH's parenthesis",
    "  depth after it (null when none).",
    "names (optional; checked only when present): the words and quoted identifiers (without quotes, a doubled closing quote read as one)",
    "  outside comments and strings, distinct, as written, in order of first appearance. Keywords count. Left out: placeholders,",
    "  numbers, a word written directly against a quote (a string prefix: N'', E'', X'', _utf8'', q''), and @ words.",
    "orderBy: whether ORDER then BY (comments between allowed) appear outside parentheses.",
    "offsetFetchOrTop: whether OFFSET, FETCH or TOP appears outside parentheses.",
    "Rules: a placeholder is : then [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*, where the colon is not part of :: and the character before it is not a",
    "  letter, digit, _, ], ) or a quote (' \" `). Words start with a letter or _ (SQL Server also #) and go on with letters, digits, _",
    "  and $ (SQL Server and Oracle also #). Per UTF-16 code unit: a letter is Unicode category L (\\p{L}; not Nl, so Ⅷ is none),",
    "  a digit is category Nd, and white space is .NET's char.IsWhiteSpace (Unicode White_Space, U+0085 included) plus U+FEFF.",
    "Skipped per dialect: -- comments and /* */ comments everywhere (nested in postgresql and sqlserver); '...' with '' everywhere;",
    "  postgresql: E'...' with backslash escapes, $$...$$ and $tag$...$tag$, \"...\" identifiers; sqlserver: [...] with ]],",
    "  \"...\" identifiers; mysql: # comments, '...' and \"...\" strings with backslash escapes, `...` identifiers; sqlite: [...]",
    "  (no escape), `...` and \"...\" identifiers; oracle: q'x...x' with [] {} () <> pairs, \"...\" identifiers. An unclosed comment,",
    "  string or identifier runs to the end.",
    "finalSemicolon (optional; checked only when present): the offset of the text's final ; (the last token outside comments,",
    "  strings and quoted identifiers, when it is a ; outside parentheses; only white space and comments follow it), or null."
  ],
